terminal, possibly useful in 789 chow or all terminals/honors, but we\u2019re far from such patterns. Slightly riskier than T5 but acceptable.\n- **Play B7**: We have two B7s. This is a pair. Discarding one breaks the pair, which could be useful for future kong or pair wait. B7 was used in a chi by us earlier ([B6,B7,B8]), indicating it might be somewhat visible. But two remain unshown. Risky to discard as it may complete others\u2019 chows (e.g., 567, 678, 789).\n\nBest options: **Play T5** (safest, least useful to opponents, neutral tile), **Play W9** or **Play W7** (mid-to-late game, avoid feeding chows).\n\nReason:  \nT5 is a simple tile in a suit where we have no other representatives, making it structurally useless to us. It\u2019s also abundant in the wall (3 left), reducing scarcity risk. Compared to B3, B9, B7, or F3\u2014which could feed chows or have wind/dragon significance\u2014T5 poses minimal danger and preserves flexibility. While W7 or W9 are also playable, T5 is more neutral.\n\nAnswer: Play T5"}
